hreat. White has isolated stones at G8 and I8. The best move is to disrupt Black\'s formation by taking H6, blocking the downward extension and asserting control near the center.\n\nReason: H6 prevents Black from easily extending their vertical three, reduces their potential for creating a double threat, and is strategically close to White\'s existing stone at G8.\n\nAnswer: {"col": "H", "row": 6}'}
